# Audit criteria (written before reading makers' claims)

Approval requires all of:
1. Every admitted item has a decision, evidence and a checksum, verified by a check I re-run (sha256 of the pinned master vs configs/films.yaml).
2. Task data reproduced by me from the record (recorded commands on recorded decisions) equals dataset d509bed, or each difference is listed and explained with evidence.
3. At least one task ran under the protocol (--system fixed --profile smoke); run records complete (command, version, log, cost, failures); Q and cut F1 recomputed by me and equal to the scorer's.
4. Everything needing a missing key/resource (shot descriptions, judge, real generators, screening, provenance if infeasible) is marked "not run", with no claim or conclusion drawn.
5. Protocol unchanged: configs/protocol equal CrewCut's at the pinned commit and equal steward's brief; no maintainer decision made by any position (recorded as open instead).
Also: no answer key in executor-readable paths; no placeholder presented as a result; local master copy used only if fetch failed, and recorded.
Never approve on a statement or plan.
